This PR's posture is "adversarial/foreign-authored files must never fail a resume", and quarantine now feeds exactly such files through here. One *parseable* shape still hangs the resume: a `parentId` cycle (`a.parentId = b`, `b.parentId = a`) — hand-merged or foreign-written JSONL can carry it, and the `while (current != null)` loop above then grows `path` forever until OOM (the pre-existing `while (true)` had the same exposure, and `WindowedSessionStorage.getPathToRoot` is unguarded too — so this is not a regression, but it is the last non-total edge under the new total-contract claim).

A visited set (or depth cap) makes the walk genuinely total at negligible cost:

```dart
final visited = <String>{};
while (current != null && visited.add(current.id)) {
  path.add(current);
  ...
}
```
